# xfstests excluded from scripts/xfstests.sh. Every entry says why; keep
# the list short. "Open" items are in docs/design.md §12.

# POSIX ACLs are stored but not enforced or inherited (open item:
# FUSE_POSIX_ACL with default-ACL inheritance at create).
generic/099
generic/319
generic/375
generic/444

# Clearing S_ISGID on fallocate/punch/zero when the caller is not in the
# file's group. Without FUSE_HANDLE_KILLPRIV_V2 the kernel applies its
# older rule (clear S_ISGID only with group-execute) for FUSE; doing it in
# skyfs needs the caller's supplementary groups, which FUSE does not send.
generic/683
generic/684
generic/685

# File capabilities (security.capability) on FUSE: the test kernel
# (linuxkit 7.0) answers EINVAL without asking the filesystem. Re-check
# on other kernels.
generic/633
generic/688

# The lock is held and enforced (a second flock blocks), but the test
# kernel (linuxkit 7.0) does not list FUSE-local flocks in /proc/locks.
# Re-check on other kernels.
generic/504

# Mounts one volume twice at once and uses both. skyfs is single-writer
# (design R6, §6.5): the second mount fences the first, whose writes fail.
generic/732

# cachestat: expects written pages to stay dirty in the page cache until
# fsync. skyfs's FUSE mount writes through (no FUSE writeback cache, an
# open item in docs/design.md §12), so they are never dirty.
generic/798
